WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.750 align:start position:0%
 
over the years the sniper elite series  has given players the ability to truly  see inside the minds of fascist forces  from world war ii  these games have worked through each  title to expand the tools customization  and play styles that you can use and  sniper elite 5 continues to build on  those ideas even further we spent two  hours shooting nazis in their naughty  bits on one fairly expansive level and  here's the good and the bad from our  preview hit that subscribe button give  us the old thumbs up and let's get to it  sniper elite 5 so far has a decent list  of sniper rifles submachine guns and  pistols a few of them lean experimental  and developers said they're working with  among other places the royal armories  notorious for debunking the realism of  video game guns on our channel with our  firearms expert react series we'll have  to get jonathan's reactions to these  weapons for better or worse these world  war ii guns have many customization  options and you can go find workbenches  on each level and tinker with them that  means you aren't stuck with the weapons  you load in with and can adapt your  playstyle mid mission most of the  customization feels pretty tasteful with  more period appropriate stocks raps and  scopes and suppressors which okay they  were not so common at that time this  will be good for players just looking to  have fun and don't get too distracted by  the idea of customization in world war  ii if you're more of a weapons purist a  few things might bother you front grips  do seem kind of just glued on there and  there's a variety of ammo types  including non-lethal bullets think metal  gear just very gamey we didn't see  anything else egregious though like red  dot sights guns now have iron sights  making it easy to go between precision  and a wider field of view for better  awareness although i found them to be  just a tad fiddly using a controller  this is something i could probably have  fixed in the menu and not an issue with  mouse and keyboard outside of weapons  there's a bunch of characters you can  unlock by playing through the game the  reason for this level of customization  is the game's desire to open up a lot of  different play styles in the  presentation developers said they're  going for a big sandbox where you could  do things like sit back and snipe do run  and gun stealth or just go in weapons  blazing if you want to try that we  attempted all of these styles and some  worked out better than others the level  we played occupied residents is pretty  massive with lots of different terrain  like farmland underground bunkers and a  huge compound the map also has a good  amount of vertical space with vines to  climb and zip lines for traversal the  main thing that stands out about  occupied residents are mechanics that  add replayability the level had multiple  starting places that you could find and  unlock it had routes that you could  discover and open up in multiple ways  there was also lore and intelligence  that give you optional side targets and  even some mysteries and puzzles for  example you might find a chest on one  side of the level and then the crowbar  to open it on the other side or you  might find a bunker that you can blow  open loudly or go find the guard that  has the key so you can open it without  alerting enemies at one point i blew  open a wall safe never quite found out  what was in it because i got swarmed  right after that and it was nowhere near  any objective that was my biggest  takeaway from this level there's a lot  to discover and it feels like it was  almost designed like hitman for you to  replay it over and over and perfect your  runs and that takes us back to  non-lethal ammo i'm willing to bet there  are non-lethal playthroughs and  achievements associated with it in  general they're now just a host of  non-lethal options and those takedowns  are fun they're even more effective  sometimes than guns and it's pretty  satisfying to whistle at an enemy get  their attention draw them over and then  drop a haymaker  on the hitman esque front there are  plenty of environmental kills too like  dropping chandeliers and supplies on  people there's also a huge variety of  red things to explode and the ability to  mine or booby trap both vehicles and  down soldiers  when it came to enemies the ai in this  preview was a mixed bag the way i  remember it i went back and played  sniper elite four so don't quote me on  this but you could pretty much do  whatever you wanted within confined  areas and the rest of the map wouldn't  get alerted in elite 5 there's still  section off places but also roving  patrols and once you go past a certain  alert level larger portions of the map  seem to come to life become far more  aggressive and chase you down some areas  didn't appear to be clearable at all  with a loud approach and enemies either  seemed to respawn or there were just too  many of them it was hard to tell the  really cool part of larger enemy map  awareness though is your ability to  manipulate where they go with careful  planning or in my case accidental  planning in one run i set up a mine very  early on and then like 20 minutes later  when i'd forgotten about it i was being  cornered by enemy troops and it went off  all the soldiers chasing me then ran to  the other side of the map and i got away  where enemy ai falls apart a bit was  once the map has gone into two high  levels of alarm huge packs of enemies  would just sort of rove into your area  and usually find you the game didn't do  as good a job at communicating how they  knew exactly where you were typically in  the sniper elite series there's a ghost  image that shows your last known  position and that's where they go but  there was really no way to know where  these giant packs of soldiers would roam  so you would usually get discovered  another place the difficulty in ai  didn't really work as well were indoors  where the cramped camera made it hard to  know exactly when it was safe to round a  corner or enter a room without being  immediately seen on the bright side you  can actually use this to your advantage  like funneling multiple bad guys into  doorways or calling them over to the  same set of bushes and repeatedly  knocking them out  one soldier ran right in front of me to  check out a decoy i just put down and  completely ignored me standing right  there again some of this is just to let  players have fun it's not necessarily  game breaking it's just something to  consider another behavior i don't  remember seeing in other sniper elite  games as much although again my  experience is more limited so tell me if  i'm wrong is multiple enemy injury  states wounded enemies would lay on the  ground and continue to spot you or  stumble around a bit after being hit it  was really cool and i felt kind of bad  in some cases for not making a clean  kill in summary the enemy of the game is  great most of the time but could  probably use some tweaks at higher alert  settings the sniping part of sniper  elite is as fantastic as ever with those  signature free anatomy lessons you get  each killcam i was able to use terrain  and the environment to great advantage  including taking out a truck driver and  then hiding out under the vehicle to  shoot down a road  there are also a decent number of  materials you can shoot through but that  cuts both ways so if you go hide in say  a tower enemies can blast through the  wood and still get you there are  multiple ammo types that play into the  system with advantages and disadvantages  armor piercing can go through metal and  stone soft points do far more damage to  troops but can't go through helmets or  wood and subsonic rounds are quieter  with less of a chance to alert but also  do less damage then there's match ammo  that has less bullet drop and  non-lethal as mentioned before the  unlock tree is fairly robust for this  kind of game there's three categories  which are combat equipment and body i  immediately went to one that lets you  pull out your pistol when you're in a  down state and it saved me multiple  times it's an unlocked tree that seems  more accommodating to a wide variety of  playstyles notice the theme going here  like more aggressive players or stealth  players i'd have to spend more time with  it to see how truly useful it is you are  pretty powerful from the start and the  game is forgiving already allowing you  to self-revive as long as you have a med  pack so again this all feels designed to  open up multiple runs of each map at  higher and higher difficulty levels  the sound design and music are really  excellent the game felt like a caper  with music swelling at the right times  or adding suspense when you were  sneaking it was really cool and when you  shoot a rifle that sound wave travels  off into the distance it's just really  satisfying  the other thing to mention is i spotted  an invasion phone which is used to give  you hints at where an invading player  kind of like dark souls might be but we  didn't actually get to see this mode yet  the plot isn't worth spending a lot of  time on kind of boils down to stop nazi  from getting super weapon and that's not  really what sniper elite players come to  this series for anyway it's just all  about that long range shooting the  mission that we played though was the  second mission with the game taking  place around d-day d-day happening  somewhere in the middle of the plot  sniper elite 5 is out on may 26th and  gamespot has a lot more coverage to go  of this and other shooter titles head on  over to gamespot and gamespot's youtube  page for firearms expert reacts  weaponless videos and our thoughts on  what's going on on major titles like  call of duty battlefield and fortnite  which is still good all right thanks for  watching  you

